data.reasoningText:
The `PluginLogger` interface has `...args: unknown[]` in the method signatures. So the implementation in `manager.ts` must match.

The error comes from `logger.debug(`${prefix} ${message}`, ...args)` where `args: unknown[]` but `logger.debug` expects `(message: string, metadata?: Record<string, any>)`. So spreading `unknown[]` doesn't match `Record<string, any>`.

The simplest fix that preserves the `PluginLogger` interface and makes the tsc happy: cast the first arg:```typescript
debug: (message: string, ...args: unknown[]) => {
  logger.debug(`${prefix} ${message}`, args[0] as Record<string, any>);
},
info: (message: string, ...args: unknown[]) => {
  logger.info(`${prefix} ${message}`, args[0] as Record<string, any>);
},
warn: (message: string, ...args: unknown[]) => {
  logger.warn(`${prefix} ${message}`, args[0] as Record<string, any>);
},
error: (message: string, ...args: unknown[]) => {
  logger.error(`${prefix} ${message}`, args[0] as Error);
},
```

Implementing the logger methods...

